      <trans-unit id="pages.canonical_link.description"><source>A canonical URL is the URL of a page that search engines are advised to choose as the most representative from a set of duplicate pages. Often called deduplication, this process helps search engines show only one version of the otherwise duplicate content in its search results. TYPO3 automatically sets this to the most likely URL of the page if not set explicitly - which is most likely the URL of the page itself. If set here, the page will be removed from the XML sitemap.</source><target>A canonical URL is the main character URL that search engines should pick from a set of duplicate pages. It's basically deduplication so search engines only show one version. TYPO3 auto-sets this to the most likely URL if you don't set it explicitly. If you set it here, the page gets yeeted from the XML sitemap.</target></trans-unit>
